"""bench-v12-audit E-e -- QLoRA fine-tune feasibility smoke on Kaggle T4.

Pre-reg: kaggle/PREREG-BENCH-V12-AUDIT.md section E-e (frozen 2026-09-26).
Question: the LARGEST Qwen3 that can be QLoRA fine-tuned on Kaggle T4 at our
sequence lengths (4096, 8192), plus the round trip back into our inference
stack (LoRA -> merged -> GGUF Q4 -> the kernel's llama.cpp llama-server).

Flow (every phase time-guarded, EE_BUDGET_MIN total):
  0. env log (nvidia-smi, torch, disk, RAM); start a CPU build of llama-quantize
     from llama.cpp tag b10636 (== the attached llama-server build) in background.
  1. pip-install a pinned unsloth stack WITHOUT touching the image's torch
     (constraints file pins torch/torchvision/torchaudio to what is installed).
  2. trials (each in its own subprocess, so an OOM cannot poison the next):
       14B dynamic-4bit, ONE T4: seq 4096 x10 steps, 8192 x10 steps
       14B plain-4bit, ONE T4: only the seqs the dynamic quant failed
       8B  (fallback ONLY if no 14B passes 4096)
       32B plain-4bit, BOTH T4s via a SUPPORTED split (unsloth
           device_map="balanced"; else HF+peft device_map="auto") -- only if
           14B passed 4096; seq 4096 x5, 8192 x3.
  3. round trip for the largest passing model:
       <=14B: unsloth save_pretrained_merged(16bit) -> convert_hf_to_gguf ->
              llama-quantize Q4_K_M -> llama-server loads it -> 1 completion.
       32B  : merged fp16 (~65 GB) does not fit Kaggle disk -> LoRA ->
              convert_lora_to_gguf -> llama-server (our Qwen3-32B Q4_K_S GGUF)
              --lora -> completion with LoRA scale 1 and 0.
     If time remains after a 32B round trip, the 14B merged round trip runs too.

Training rows are SYNTHETIC: real arm-B prompts built from the OLD gf180
library kaggle/editcap-lib-v1a (non-bench-v1.2) + archived v1-baseline
completions, padded to an exact length (see build_rows.py). No bench-v1.2 cell
or claude-solutions template is ever used (held-out fence).

No repo clone, no GH token: the rows are embedded below. Outputs (small only)
in /kaggle/working/ee/; all large artifacts live in /tmp (not kernel output).
"""
